{"name":"Trevi Fountain","hex":"#c2dfe2","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fountain","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A natural source of water; a spring.","An artificial, usually ornamental, water feature (usually in a garden or public place) consisting of one or more streams of water originating from a statue or other structure."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To flow or gush as if from a fountain."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fountain"}],"entries":[{"title":"Trevi Fountain","blocks":[{"text":"The Trevi Fountain is an 18th-century fountain in the Trevi district in Rome, Italy, designed by Italian architect Nicola Salvi and completed by Giuseppe Pannini in 1762. Standing 26.3 metres (86 ft) high and 49.15 metres (161.3 ft) wide, it is the largest Baroque fountain in the world and one of the most famous fountains in the world."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Trevi_Fountain_-_Roma.jpg/330px-Trevi_Fountain_-_Roma.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trevi_Fountain"},{"title":"Trevi (rione of Rome)","blocks":[{"text":"Trevi is the 2nd rione of Rome, Italy, identified by the initials R. II, located in Municipio I. The origin of its name is not clear, but the most accepted theory is that it comes from the Latin trivium, because there were three streets all leading to the current Piazza dei Crociferi, a square next to the modern Trevi square. Its coat of arms is made of three swords on a red background."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Trevi-Brunnen_abends.jpg/330px-Trevi-Brunnen_abends.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trevi_(rione_of_Rome)"},{"title":"Fountain","blocks":[{"text":"A fountain, from the Latin \"fons\", meaning source or spring, is a decorative reservoir used for discharging water. It is also a structure that jets water into the air for a decorative or dramatic effect in landscapes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Fountains_Collage.jpg/330px-Fountains_Collage.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fountain"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Pannini%2C_Giovanni_Paolo_-_Fountain_of_Trevi%2C_Rome_-_18th_c.jpg/500px-Pannini%2C_Giovanni_Paolo_-_Fountain_of_Trevi%2C_Rome_-_18th_c.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Pannini%2C_Giovanni_Paolo_-_Fountain_of_Trevi%2C_Rome_-_18th_c.jpg/500px-Pannini%2C_Giovanni_Paolo_-_Fountain_of_Trevi%2C_Rome_-_18th_c.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Trevi Fountain in the 18th century, painted by G. P. Panini","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APannini%2C_Giovanni_Paolo_-_Fountain_of_Trevi%2C_Rome_-_18th_c.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Lalande%2C_Joseph_Jerome_Le_Fran%C3%A7ais_de_%E2%80%93_Voyage_d%27un_fran%C3%A7ois_en_Italie%2C_fait_dans_les_ann%C3%A9es_1765_et_1766._Atlas%2C_1769_%E2%80%93_BEIC_6417616_Roma_Fontana_Trevi.jpg/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Lalande%2C_Joseph_Jerome_Le_Fran%C3%A7ais_de_%E2%80%93_Voyage_d%27un_fran%C3%A7ois_en_Italie%2C_fait_dans_les_ann%C3%A9es_1765_et_1766._Atlas%2C_1769_%E2%80%93_BEIC_6417616_Roma_Fontana_Trevi.jpg/500px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The fountain in Journey of a Frenchman in Italy (1769) by J. Lalande","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALalande%2C_Joseph_Jerome_Le_Fran%C3%A7ais_de_%E2%80%93_Voyage_d'un_fran%C3%A7o